{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the head outcome recovery design at head 9a835622862172c98d6e44316d234161067ad4da, tree 3a06c484, for request f0bdea6f, ruling f15b9b44 and review request 216f5338. This reviews the diff from 495c02f9. Verdict: APPROVED, for the design only.\n\nThis approval releases no implementation, query, room, retry, Check, Continue, provider call or token operation. It doesn't close whole-S1. Both S1 rooms stay stopped.\n\n## The three items of review b8347678\n\n1. Telemetry: resolved. The plan names the Worker, the lane scopes, the query windows, each query's filters and caps, and what each sink cannot show. I checked its figures against the sealed unit:\n   - `ae-r1.json` has 111 rows, `ae-r2.json` 89, `ae-window.json` 34 and `q0.json` 26 groups.\n   - In `q0.json`, the points sum to 1,456 metric-dropped and 936 others. `ae-dropped.json` reports 1,457. The plan keeps both.\n   - `logs-r1.json` has 110 archive events and one other, the RPC-stub warning. `logs-r2.json` has 45 archive events and no such warning.\n   - `Diagnosis` holds request, event, step and name, with no scope or operation field, as the plan says.\n2. The blind spot: resolved. The plan states that an empty result clears nothing, that a third unknown would be as blind, and that the reader adds no stage evidence. It records request 4f3336c1, which puts fixed-stage diagnosis first.\n3. Status lines: resolved. Both now describe scope and not a review state, and \"Root\" no longer appears in either document.\n\nThe plan corrects one of my own citations. My item 2 cited `artifacts-host.ts:262` and `:269` beside the head path. Those lines are in `createRepository`. The head path is `ref` at `:339-340`, through `#read` at `:397-414`. The plan cites both correctly, and it says that the `createRepository` catches are no evidence about either head attempt.\n\n## The retention qualification you asked me to assess\n\nIt holds. The plan says that the planner did not check this account's limits, and it gives Cloudflare's published limits as public references that don't identify this account's settings. It infers no effective limit. It also says that a count below a query cap doesn't prove complete ingestion, and the sealed bytes need no future retention. The sealed unit answers only for the bounded windows that it covers. The plan says so, so nothing further is needed for this design.\n\n## The shortened passages\n\nThe diff shortens the reader's rationale, the selected-policy section and the old evidence table. Each surviving passage keeps its limit:\n\n- only an attempt's own answer can follow an unknown, and a fresh read cannot;\n- a provider ID or an operator label is not proof;\n- a fresh observation needs Choice B's separate review.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree holds this head and is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto 0f0a949e gives the head tree 3a06c484. Main has since moved to 9ad5ae93, and the merge onto it has no conflict and gives tree ce51fae8, because S2's paths don't overlap this head's.\n- The head changes four documentation paths from 0f0a949e, and the four artifacts match. They may read stale for the same reason as in the last review.\n- The evidence verifies:\n  - the telemetry unit has 14 files and 418,806 bytes, its `SHA256SUMS` has digest 8c4f9c5d and reruns clean, and no file is writable;\n  - the manifest has SHA-256 71c19553, and its rows match the retained files and this head's documents and source files.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 774 links, 0 broken. check-notes from 0f0a949e: 0 warnings. check-commit-messages: 4 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` from 495c02f9: clean.\n- No gate ran, and the documents-only rule allows that: only documents differ from main.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The sealed `q0.json` shows that metric-dropped points outnumber all others on `dap-demo`. Request 4f3336c1 owns the cause. Until then, a missing metric point says little.\n2. Plan 034 still carries a long reader contract for a service that has no store, and that may answer `answer-unavailable` for both rooms. Implementation should revisit it after the diagnosis work reports.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe order is now right: diagnosis first, then any reader or new attempt under its own request. The plan adds nothing to the kernel and leaves section 7 to govern later work. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nThe plan keeps credentials and bodies out of output, limits live sink queries to an authorized account operator, and sets the `diag.ts` redaction rule for the later diagnosis. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe diff shortens the reader's rationale and replaces a table of hypotheticals with what the sinks showed. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: all three items of b8347678 are resolved, ruling f15b9b44's question now has a concrete answer, and the evidence holds. The answer is that the sealed telemetry doesn't identify the cause.\n- Landing this head deploys nothing, because it changes only documents.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8f9c103d218430d80222fbe021a2b4bba78d00b8","binding":"assigned","head":"9a835622862172c98d6e44316d234161067ad4da","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:be6033f73157f3ea7f5456c39707090e1bb39a27\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bdf11579925ae3f045796a3bfab3a8b045b25c2e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:54ddcdc1ee02c5ce540ac3f4811a2e8dcfc5ac85","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:100fcfe020a1db971ad69b356705db010a3188f6, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:216f5338ea97cab1920cf66da58c77f1000bf0a1, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d5